<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of 1812</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1812–1815</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of 1812 was fought from 1812 to 1815 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the United Kingdom, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s Canadian colonies and Native American allies. Provoked by British trade restrictions and the impressment of American sailors, it saw failed American invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, the burning of Washington (1814) and an American victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> (1815); the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a> restored the pre-war borders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-1812.jpg" alt="War of 1812" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clockwise, from top: George Munger, John David Kelly, Anton Otto Fischer, William Emmons, Edward Percy Moran · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:War_of_1812_Montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
